      "content": "The serpentine belt, also known as the accessory drive belt, powers many of your vehicle's systems by moving from one pulley to another. It could make a screeching sound if it's worn, improperly tensioned, or if it’s rubbing against something due to misalignment. While it could be related, it's more likely that other components, such as the drive belts (for the alternator, power steering pump, etc.), are causing the noise. It’s best to consult a professional mechanic to diagnose and fix the issue.",
